                                "sense_id": "781f39b3-a05f-35d0-b3c6-c0b227d11343",
                                "text": "It was really fine, the first part in Australia, the two last in China, the latter particularly good, the burning of the English factories in Canton quite life-like, the Chinese buildings well portrayed, and those fellows, those rat-eating, chop-sticky, pig-tailed Chinamen, have an idea or two about living."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8fbf677f-dcb0-4c5b-8acc-da35ad61271b",
                                "sense_id": "781f39b3-a05f-35d0-b3c6-c0b227d11343",
                                "text": "Old pigtailed seamen would tell of horseshoes found in the meat casks; of curious barkings and neighings heard in the slaughter-houses; and of negroes who disappeared near the victualling yards, to be seen no more."
                            }
